<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Reforma</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Reform era</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Reforma was a period of liberal reform in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> that began after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolution-of-ayutla">Revolution of Ayutla</a> overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a> in 1855. Laws such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ley-juarez">Ley Juárez</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ley-lerdo">Ley Lerdo</a> curtailed the legal privileges of the Church and the army and forced the sale of corporate lands, and the Constitution of 1857 enshrined these principles. Conservative resistance led to the Reform War of 1858–1861 and helped prepare the way for French intervention.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-reforma.jpg" alt="La Reforma" width="320" height="515" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petronilo Monroy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alegor%C3%ADa_de_la_Constituci%C3%B3n_de_1857.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
